WEBVTT

00:26.760 --> 00:31.060
Spaceship Kudryavka is within
900 meters of the docking area.

00:47.640 --> 00:50.810
Kudryavka is within 300 meters.

01:47.270 --> 01:51.100
Doi-san, you always get sick
when you come out to space.

01:51.210 --> 01:53.040
I'm so ashamed.

02:09.220 --> 02:13.130
Well? What do you think
of our special space curry?

02:14.460 --> 02:17.460
Try to come up with
something better next time!

02:19.430 --> 02:20.400
Hey!

02:20.470 --> 02:25.870
But, Noguchi-san, even if this
does help our bones stay strong...

02:25.970 --> 02:28.380
...this stuff's too disgusting!

02:28.480 --> 02:32.470
We've been living
here for four years now.

02:34.280 --> 02:38.980
Plus there's a time limit to the
artificial gravity, and in zero gravity...

02:39.420 --> 02:46.690
...we don't know how much bone
mass is lost and calcium dissolved.

02:49.600 --> 02:52.800
This curry isn't that bad.

02:53.370 --> 02:57.700
Did you forget who got
urolithiasis and spasms last year...

02:57.810 --> 03:01.370
...because of calcium
that wouldn't dissolve?

03:02.280 --> 03:05.680
When you return to Earth,
your bones will be worn out.

03:05.780 --> 03:08.080
That wouldn't be funny at all.

03:09.750 --> 03:11.650
Defy Food Company...

03:11.750 --> 03:15.250
No, Doi-san's space food...

03:15.360 --> 03:19.820
We should all understand by
now how important it is to us.

03:20.930 --> 03:23.260
I've been researching a long time...

03:23.370 --> 03:27.270
...on how to strengthen
the bones with space food.

03:27.370 --> 03:30.170
Well, I can't say
I'm a first-class chef...

03:30.270 --> 03:36.110
...but this food is landmark,
historic, and revolutionary, everyone!

03:41.320 --> 03:46.520
Blood composition and
muscle atrophy is normal.

03:46.760 --> 03:48.420
Bone density...

03:48.620 --> 03:54.490
Calcium, phosphorus, and
magnesium levels are unchanged.

03:55.100 --> 04:00.470
But the volume of bone
has gone up twenty percent.

04:01.140 --> 04:04.770
Doi-san, this is really something.

04:04.870 --> 04:08.040
Your special space food, that is.

04:08.940 --> 04:12.610
Thank you very much.
Well, it's kind of obvious.

04:14.180 --> 04:15.150
What?

04:15.220 --> 04:16.650
Space radiation?

04:17.120 --> 04:21.220
The amount of radiation exposure
is based on individual data...

04:21.320 --> 04:24.020
...and we've done
a lot of stuff in space...

04:24.130 --> 04:28.260
...so we shouldn't be the only
ones with high levels of radiation.

04:29.160 --> 04:32.930
This year, when the sun's
radiation was being emitted...

04:33.030 --> 04:38.470
...the only crew sent out on
missions were you two, Noguchi-san.

04:38.940 --> 04:41.810
Then it must be from solar flares.

04:42.910 --> 04:43.970
Great.

04:44.080 --> 04:48.980
Weren't the spacesuits supposed
to block any type of space radiation?

04:49.550 --> 04:54.250
Can you two not go out
on missions for a while?

04:54.360 --> 04:56.550
Oh, just in case.

04:56.890 --> 05:01.260
This isn't because of the space
food I created, right, Doctor?

05:02.430 --> 05:06.260
No one said it was your fault.

05:08.440 --> 05:11.700
My daughter's birthday
is coming up soon.

05:12.170 --> 05:18.080
I'm sure Monaka's room
is filled with your presents.

05:18.910 --> 05:22.180
I can't be there to see her grow up.

05:22.450 --> 05:26.150
This is the toughest thing for a father.

05:28.060 --> 05:30.550
I haven't seen her in four years.

05:31.330 --> 05:36.290
If I'm not mistaken, your younger
brother is looking after Monaka.

05:37.130 --> 05:42.660
After my wife passed away, I went
back to work on the space station.

05:43.670 --> 05:47.200
I had no choice but
to leave her with my brother.

05:47.710 --> 05:50.800
I want you to give
the present to her, Doi.

05:51.110 --> 05:54.610
I understand.
I'll make sure to deliver it to her.

06:00.090 --> 06:02.720
Monaka, happy birthday.

06:33.090 --> 06:34.320
Bastard!

06:34.960 --> 06:36.290
Move it!

06:44.670 --> 06:45.630
Sorry!

06:54.280 --> 06:57.840
Ambulance right now!
We'll pursue the suspect!

06:57.950 --> 06:59.210
Damn it...

07:25.970 --> 07:26.980
Hey!

07:26.980 --> 07:28.340
Police!

07:29.740 --> 07:31.180
Same here!

07:57.840 --> 07:59.140
Tsuin!

08:00.010 --> 08:01.870
If you come in, I'll kill her.

08:06.350 --> 08:09.280
Let the hostage go! I'll take her place!

08:15.160 --> 08:16.280
Damn...

08:16.390 --> 08:18.490
Gaga, call the negotiator.

08:19.160 --> 08:22.790
We can't negotiate with that pervert!

08:23.130 --> 08:24.460
Let's get him!

08:24.570 --> 08:28.330
That's up to the department.
Wait 'till backup comes.

08:29.170 --> 08:34.070
He has that little girl hostage!
If we don't get him soon, she'll be...

08:34.680 --> 08:37.910
No one can get in here for a while.

08:40.250 --> 08:41.310
No!

08:41.420 --> 08:42.940
No!

08:43.150 --> 08:44.640
Let me go!

08:44.750 --> 08:48.550
You're gonna stay with me
'till I reach a safer place.

08:50.190 --> 08:51.890
Let me go!

08:52.160 --> 08:54.930
No! No!

08:55.060 --> 08:57.190
Don't touch me, you pervert!

09:30.500 --> 09:32.430
Who the hell are you?

09:35.900 --> 09:37.300
Who are you?

09:44.280 --> 09:45.710
Close it.

09:50.320 --> 09:51.840
A woman?

09:58.790 --> 10:00.020
Hey, wait!

10:04.400 --> 10:05.490
No way...

10:05.600 --> 10:06.730
Hey, Tsuin!

10:09.340 --> 10:11.740
This is why we should've busted him!

10:12.070 --> 10:13.340
Let's go!

10:23.720 --> 10:24.840
Tsuin...

10:25.890 --> 10:27.950
What the hell happened?

10:39.830 --> 10:43.030
You're safe now.
You must've been scared.

10:43.670 --> 10:45.640
But you're safe now.

10:48.210 --> 10:49.800
The Angel of Death.

10:50.350 --> 10:54.540
I'm the stationmaster,
but even I can't do that kind of thing.

10:55.550 --> 10:57.250
Don't talk nonsense.

10:57.890 --> 11:03.450
The suspect who killed Tsuin might
still be somewhere in this station!

11:03.560 --> 11:06.990
Hurry up and close
the station and stop all the trains!

11:07.100 --> 11:09.790
Don't let any passengers out!

12:25.110 --> 12:28.080
I'll come by again for
that nice ass of yours.

12:33.620 --> 12:35.810
“The customer is always right.“

12:36.850 --> 12:38.080
Smile. Smile.

12:38.350 --> 12:40.320
Spicy Habanero.

12:41.090 --> 12:42.350
Smile.

12:45.190 --> 12:46.820
Thanks for waiting!

12:47.460 --> 12:50.360
Make yourself at home.

13:01.340 --> 13:06.280
He had stomach cramps, Mukai.
This is obstruction of business.

13:06.380 --> 13:10.340
I don't ever want to see
that kind of customer again.

13:11.420 --> 13:13.440
Sorry I'm late.

13:14.060 --> 13:17.460
Monaka!
I feel relieved when I see you.

13:19.030 --> 13:22.760
Hey, there's a customer.
Go get their order.

13:22.960 --> 13:23.930
Right!

13:30.270 --> 13:32.170
You're so clumsy.

13:32.970 --> 13:34.600
Get up quickly.

13:34.710 --> 13:35.970
I'm sorry.

13:39.810 --> 13:40.780
Welcome!

13:41.520 --> 13:43.480
What would you like?

13:43.750 --> 13:48.550
The demi-glace jumbo hamburger
set and a large caesar salad.

13:48.990 --> 13:50.960
Hey, are you listening?

13:51.060 --> 13:54.150
Let me conﬁrm your order.
The dam-ghee...

13:54.260 --> 13:55.290
Hey!

13:56.100 --> 13:57.390
I'm sorry.

13:57.500 --> 14:00.160
She's still new.

14:01.240 --> 14:04.500
Hey, go tell them
this customer's order.

14:04.610 --> 14:05.940
R-Right.

14:11.250 --> 14:13.980
Mr. Manager,
I'm sorry to have troubled you...

14:14.080 --> 14:16.050
That customer before was...

14:18.050 --> 14:22.320
If they find out I'm working
a minor like you late at night...

14:22.420 --> 14:26.330
...I'm the one who's gonna get busted.

14:27.300 --> 14:32.320
You'd better not get your business
license suspended, Manager.

14:33.430 --> 14:36.500
Ow! That hurt, Mukai!

14:37.070 --> 14:41.300
Noguchi-san, if he sexually harasses
you, then you'd better say so.

14:42.540 --> 14:43.810
I don't mind.

14:44.050 --> 14:45.270
You should.

14:45.380 --> 14:49.320
After all, it's not like he's
doing anything outrageous...

14:53.220 --> 14:53.920
Yeah?

14:53.920 --> 14:55.220
Yeah?
Leave now.

14:55.290 --> 14:56.850
I'm still working.

14:56.960 --> 15:00.220
I don't have your stuff ready yet.

15:01.530 --> 15:03.360
My brother's dead...

15:05.000 --> 15:08.830
My only sweet little
brother has been killed.

15:09.370 --> 15:10.340
What?

15:33.660 --> 15:35.820
ID confirmed. Welcome home.

15:49.510 --> 15:50.940
You're really late.

15:53.480 --> 15:55.110
I'm sorry.

15:55.220 --> 15:57.280
What time do you think it is?

15:57.390 --> 16:01.050
I'll let you know in advance
if I'm coming home late.

16:01.160 --> 16:02.950
Why not change jobs?

16:03.060 --> 16:09.260
But I don't want you to keep paying
for my living expenses and tuition.

16:10.100 --> 16:16.260
I don't want to pester you since I'm
also living off your father's expenses.

16:16.700 --> 16:22.770
I appreciate your concern, but doing
babysitting late at night pays a lot.

16:25.210 --> 16:29.780
It's a dangerous world. Be careful
when you're walking alone at night.

16:30.720 --> 16:31.880
I will...

16:54.980 --> 16:56.110
Can I come in?

16:56.110 --> 16:57.510
Yeah, sure.

16:57.610 --> 17:00.740
You came home really late.
I'm so sleepy now.

17:00.850 --> 17:02.250
You were waiting?

17:02.350 --> 17:04.820
I was holding on to this for you.

17:05.190 --> 17:06.350
Thanks.

17:07.490 --> 17:09.010
Can I get one?

17:09.120 --> 17:13.190
Sure, you can take
anything except matcha vanilla.

17:14.700 --> 17:15.790
Thank you!

17:18.270 --> 17:20.500
I only see matcha vanilla.

17:22.040 --> 17:24.700
I'm taking this cookie milk.

17:26.440 --> 17:28.880
You're really loved, Monaka.

17:31.850 --> 17:35.310
It says this package is
from Doi-san. Who is he?

17:35.820 --> 17:40.150
He's my father's friend,
but I don't know much about him.

17:44.330 --> 17:46.730
What is it this time?

17:46.830 --> 17:48.390
So pretty...

17:48.700 --> 17:50.030
What is it?

17:54.040 --> 17:55.900
Rocks from Mars.

17:56.570 --> 17:57.900
Awesome!

17:58.470 --> 18:01.910
You're probably the only
one in the world who has this.

18:05.410 --> 18:07.070
I'm really jealous...

18:07.180 --> 18:10.640
I want something
like that for my birthday too.

18:14.790 --> 18:16.620
It looks good on you.

18:21.160 --> 18:25.930
I guess you get remarkable things
if you have an astronaut as a father.

18:29.040 --> 18:30.730
Thank you, Dad.

18:39.380 --> 18:41.750
This swelling is abnormal.

18:42.880 --> 18:44.750
Their kidneys seem fine...

18:44.850 --> 18:48.450
...so I don't think it's due
to the movement of bodily fluids.

18:48.560 --> 18:55.900
Plus artificial gravity is working now,
and we've been living here for years.

18:56.500 --> 18:58.990
They shouldn't swell up like this.

18:59.730 --> 19:02.170
Then how do you
explain these symptoms?

19:05.670 --> 19:07.300
Monaka...

19:19.450 --> 19:20.750
Go!

19:20.890 --> 19:22.120
Fly!

19:22.860 --> 19:24.120
There!

19:27.800 --> 19:31.360
It went very high with the wind...

19:32.830 --> 19:37.400
Monaka, I'm going back up to space.

19:46.280 --> 19:48.080
Will I see you again?

19:48.580 --> 19:50.140
Of course.

19:50.420 --> 19:54.860
No matter what happens,
I'll come back to see you.

19:56.320 --> 19:58.590
I'll be waiting for you.

19:59.530 --> 20:02.760
I promise...
I promise that I'll come back.

20:07.740 --> 20:11.500
Something... Something is
about to happen inside his body...

20:26.790 --> 20:29.420
You are my shooting star...

20:30.020 --> 20:34.120
We spend the night feeling
our attraction for each other.

20:34.230 --> 20:37.030
You are my shining star...

20:37.260 --> 20:37.860
Run past the light and the body.

20:37.870 --> 20:40.330
Run past the light and the body.
Good morning! Breakfast is ready.

20:40.330 --> 20:41.670
Good morning. I'll be right down.

20:41.670 --> 20:43.400
Wish upon a star...

20:43.400 --> 20:44.460
Wish upon a star...

20:44.670 --> 20:48.870
It gets covered
like a powdery snow.

20:49.080 --> 20:52.050
Sending my thoughts to the moon...

20:52.150 --> 20:54.880
l keep waiting and...

20:56.350 --> 20:59.380
Want to hang out
with me this Sunday?

20:59.750 --> 21:01.150
Where you'll go?

21:01.260 --> 21:02.720
Karaoke!

21:02.820 --> 21:07.090
I finish work in the evening,
so we'll meet in Ikebukuro.

21:07.190 --> 21:10.990
My friends are coming too,
so you should come, Monaka!

21:11.870 --> 21:15.730
Well, I'm not really good
at singing. I'm terrible.

21:15.840 --> 21:17.630
Don't worry!

21:17.740 --> 21:22.300
It's not like everyone's really
good at it. Let's have some fun!

21:22.410 --> 21:24.140
Go with your boyfriend.

21:26.380 --> 21:28.820
We broke up two weeks ago.

21:29.120 --> 21:30.350
Seriously?

21:30.450 --> 21:34.580
I'm having a hard time recovering.
I need you to comfort me.

21:36.560 --> 21:40.490
They say meetings and
partings happen over and over.

21:40.590 --> 21:42.590
So don't be discouraged, Azuki.

21:44.800 --> 21:47.100
Monaka, ever been in love?

21:48.340 --> 21:50.030
Where'd that come from?

21:50.140 --> 21:52.970
Are there any boys you like right now?

21:53.070 --> 21:56.070
This vegetable soup is really good.

21:56.540 --> 21:58.710
That's pork and vegetables.

21:59.450 --> 22:00.570
Oink.

22:06.450 --> 22:09.820
One-bedroom apartments
are pretty expensive...

22:16.730 --> 22:19.450
We're going to have a bag check now.

22:20.300 --> 22:23.570
Take everything out of your
bags and place them on the desk.

22:23.800 --> 22:25.240
What?

22:42.420 --> 22:45.590
Where do you think we are?

22:48.630 --> 22:49.760
Noguchi.

22:49.860 --> 22:50.990
Yes?

22:52.700 --> 22:56.930
I heard you got the second
highest grade for the term exams.

22:57.040 --> 22:59.600
Try to get the best score next time.

23:00.240 --> 23:01.330
Okay.

23:21.960 --> 23:23.730
It's so far...

23:35.980 --> 23:38.340
Mukai-san had a child...

23:39.280 --> 23:41.370
That's right.
She's a single mother.

23:42.880 --> 23:44.370
Manager-san.

23:45.090 --> 23:46.850
What a surprise.

23:46.920 --> 23:49.020
What book did you buy?

23:49.420 --> 23:52.690
Eat and Lose Weight,
an Ultimate Diet!

23:52.790 --> 23:56.200
I can turn my blood
from muddy to smooth.

23:56.600 --> 23:58.330
Do your best.

23:58.430 --> 23:59.800
Yeah, I wiII.

24:00.370 --> 24:03.630
What happened to
Mukai-san's husband?

24:04.340 --> 24:05.570
Who knows...

24:05.840 --> 24:08.770
Even I don't know what happened.

24:09.040 --> 24:14.310
She won't say anything about it,
and I don't really care to know.

24:15.980 --> 24:18.920
She didn't seem like
a single mother to me...

24:19.950 --> 24:22.120
By the way, Monaka.

24:22.320 --> 24:24.310
Don't be late tonight.

24:25.990 --> 24:27.090
Okay.

24:28.060 --> 24:28.860
Good girl! So cute!

24:28.860 --> 24:30.660
Good girl! So cute!
I can't breathe!

24:35.340 --> 24:37.810
Did you find anything you like?

24:38.070 --> 24:44.340
Um, can I go and take
a look at this one right now?

24:45.050 --> 24:48.850
There are no lights,
so the room's pitch-black at night.

24:48.950 --> 24:51.180
The moonlight's enough.

24:54.290 --> 24:56.420
This is a wonderful room...

24:57.120 --> 25:01.580
They spent a lot to soundproof this
place, so you'll have plenty of privacy.

25:02.130 --> 25:04.000
That's important.

25:04.870 --> 25:08.600
Can I stay here by myself for a while?

25:09.770 --> 25:11.140
Sure.

25:21.650 --> 25:25.110
The rent's high, but you won't regret it.

25:25.650 --> 25:27.950
I don't plan to move in here.

25:42.640 --> 25:46.900
Seven people died by
your hands, but this ends now.

26:16.800 --> 26:18.430
What is this?

26:19.810 --> 26:21.240
What happened here?

26:23.980 --> 26:26.110
Anyway, let's find the crew.

26:36.020 --> 26:38.010
L-Let's go back, everyone...

26:38.130 --> 26:41.120
I have a bad feeling about this...

26:41.800 --> 26:47.000
We lost contact after hearing
gunshots and a distress signal.

26:48.070 --> 26:49.630
We can't go back.

26:53.010 --> 26:54.060
Doctor!

26:56.010 --> 26:58.880
Doctor, answer if you're here!

26:58.980 --> 27:00.910
We're from the center...

27:05.250 --> 27:06.450
Jeez.

27:06.850 --> 27:08.620
Head to the crew quarters...

27:58.040 --> 27:59.400
Doctor!

28:00.110 --> 28:02.130
Where were you, Doctor?

28:02.610 --> 28:04.700
Hang in there! Are you okay?

28:04.810 --> 28:08.250
Hurry, to the Kudryavka.
That thing is coming...

28:11.320 --> 28:15.410
Doctor, what is that monster?
What the heck happened here?

28:16.060 --> 28:17.220
Doi-san...

28:17.660 --> 28:20.090
That space food you brought here...

28:20.190 --> 28:23.360
Is it true they weren't
tested in the center labs?

28:23.700 --> 28:25.360
W-What now?

28:26.600 --> 28:31.130
That creature transformed
after eating your space food.

28:31.240 --> 28:33.300
It was once human.

28:33.540 --> 28:36.670
You must be kidding...
What are you saying, Doctor?

28:37.610 --> 28:43.410
Your space food provided way too
much stimulation on the bones.

28:43.880 --> 28:47.080
After developing rapidly
with the sun's radiation...

28:47.190 --> 28:51.420
...bones were enlarged,
turning into that creature.

28:51.890 --> 28:54.260
Do you have proof?

28:56.560 --> 28:57.790
It'll bust through!

28:57.900 --> 29:00.630
Hurry up and get to the Kudryavka!

29:09.880 --> 29:11.000
Damn it...

29:11.110 --> 29:13.910
The docking tube
will explode at this rate!

29:21.960 --> 29:24.190
Close the Kudryavka's airlock door!

29:41.940 --> 29:43.070
Lock the door!

29:45.510 --> 29:46.600
It's not working!

30:06.200 --> 30:07.790
We're saved...

30:07.900 --> 30:11.390
The fuel ignited!
Hurry up to the escape pods!

30:11.510 --> 30:12.670
What?

30:15.980 --> 30:17.710
Releasing safety lock!

30:23.780 --> 30:24.750
Take off!

30:24.850 --> 30:26.720
Please, God...

30:40.430 --> 30:42.730
We're heading into the atmosphere!

30:48.080 --> 30:49.740
Activating air brake!

31:05.690 --> 31:10.460
We can't go back to the center!
This ship will explode soon!

31:11.430 --> 31:13.090
How long 'till we land?

31:13.200 --> 31:16.190
Altitude of 4,000 meters,
1.5 minutes 'till landing!

31:16.300 --> 31:18.000
We won't make it.

31:18.110 --> 31:21.970
You'll have to force a landing.
That's the only way we'll survive.

31:33.490 --> 31:35.050
Where are we now?

31:35.160 --> 31:37.650
Who cares? Save us!

31:37.760 --> 31:39.780
Just land this thing safely!

31:39.890 --> 31:43.350
Calm down! We can't
land in the middle of the city!

31:43.460 --> 31:44.930
In the ocean!

31:47.100 --> 31:49.190
Altitude of 400 meters!

31:57.010 --> 31:58.310
We're gonna crash!

32:05.050 --> 32:08.110
Altitude of 40 meters!
We're landing on water!

32:22.670 --> 32:24.470
We're gonna plunge in!

32:33.150 --> 32:35.580
We're finally saved...

32:36.480 --> 32:38.110
Outside quickly!

32:39.020 --> 32:40.110
Move it!

32:57.340 --> 33:00.200
Thank you, God... I'm very lucky.

33:04.410 --> 33:06.540
What would you like?

33:07.350 --> 33:09.680
Coffee and a vegetable sandwich.

33:09.780 --> 33:12.550
And can you put
ketchup instead of mayo?

33:13.090 --> 33:15.650
You always order the same thing.

33:16.660 --> 33:19.090
Monaka‘s so cute...

33:20.990 --> 33:23.020
Monaka, customer!

33:24.130 --> 33:25.360
Coming!

33:25.470 --> 33:27.060
I'll do it.

33:27.170 --> 33:28.160
Not you.

33:29.470 --> 33:30.770
Welcome!

33:37.480 --> 33:38.540
No!

33:46.520 --> 33:47.750
Ouch...

33:47.850 --> 33:49.080
Y-You okay?

33:49.190 --> 33:51.420
You don't give up, do you?

33:52.360 --> 33:56.890
I wanted to see what
kind of beer I got this time.

33:58.570 --> 34:00.930
Then I'll give you something stronger.

34:09.210 --> 34:10.470
Mukai!

34:13.280 --> 34:14.540
What is it?

34:14.650 --> 34:16.340
Why you...

34:16.550 --> 34:18.040
Good job.

34:21.190 --> 34:24.050
Um, thank you very much.

34:24.560 --> 34:27.690
Noguchi-san, do you know
self-defense techniques?

34:28.930 --> 34:30.190
No...

34:30.730 --> 34:35.960
You tried to stab that
pervert with a pen, didn't you?

34:37.970 --> 34:39.940
I don't really remember.

34:40.040 --> 34:42.070
Did I do that?

34:42.610 --> 34:44.580
A conditioned reflex.

34:45.050 --> 34:47.510
You're the amazing one, Mukai-san.

34:47.610 --> 34:50.080
Did you learn
some kind of martial art?

34:52.490 --> 34:54.080
Playing dumb, huh?

34:54.190 --> 34:56.090
I'm not playing dumb.

34:56.590 --> 34:58.120
Whatever.

34:58.530 --> 35:01.190
Go get those dishes from table one.

35:01.560 --> 35:02.720
Okay!

35:14.310 --> 35:18.800
The NASA investigation
committee will assure your safety.

35:18.910 --> 35:22.910
You don't need to worry about
being questioned by the police...

35:23.020 --> 35:27.610
...and you will not say a word
about this incident from here on.

35:27.720 --> 35:29.420
Are you insane?

35:30.290 --> 35:32.850
Just leave everything to us.

35:35.000 --> 35:38.330
The truth is that there's
more than one creature.

35:38.700 --> 35:40.720
There he goes again.

35:41.640 --> 35:45.700
Either way, they became space dust.

35:46.840 --> 35:49.570
Don't tell anyone about that monster.

35:50.310 --> 35:54.010
Of the two creatures, one is Noguchi.

35:55.520 --> 35:57.680
Orudo Noguchi-san.

35:58.320 --> 35:59.650
Noguchi-san?

35:59.750 --> 36:01.080
That's right.

36:02.660 --> 36:08.460
How do you go about telling their
families what happened today?

36:24.180 --> 36:27.150
Noguchi-san, do you
have time after you change?

36:28.080 --> 36:29.520
What is it?

36:29.820 --> 36:30.980
Just to relax.

36:34.820 --> 36:37.190
You do this sometimes?

36:38.590 --> 36:41.490
It helps me remember the past...

36:42.660 --> 36:44.990
...when the lights are sparking.

36:50.100 --> 36:52.600
Fireworks in the winter are nice.

36:52.710 --> 36:54.000
Right?

36:54.310 --> 36:57.110
Noguchi-san,
do you have a boyfriend?

36:59.050 --> 37:00.540
No, I don't.

37:01.650 --> 37:02.810
I see...

37:03.720 --> 37:08.380
If you have a lover, family member,
or someone important to you...

37:08.660 --> 37:11.650
...then you have to mend
your ways, Noguchi-san.

37:12.130 --> 37:14.530
What do you mean by that?

37:16.360 --> 37:20.320
Oh my! You two are
really good friends now, huh?

37:24.800 --> 37:29.000
It's nice to do fireworks in the winter,
but don't forget to put out the fire...

37:29.110 --> 37:30.670
...Big Boss Mukai.

37:31.610 --> 37:32.770
Good work.

37:33.250 --> 37:35.910
Good work. Good night, Mr. Manager.

37:36.320 --> 37:38.480
Good night, Monaka.

37:39.550 --> 37:41.210
Oh, Mukai.

37:41.590 --> 37:44.850
The customer you
sent to the hospital...

37:44.960 --> 37:48.900
His fees will be taken out
of your paycheck this month.

37:49.000 --> 37:51.860
You want me to burn
down this restaurant?

37:52.630 --> 37:53.900
Mukai-san!

37:54.630 --> 37:56.030
Just kidding.

37:59.770 --> 38:03.710
D-Doesn't this bother
people in the neighborhood?

38:04.010 --> 38:07.670
I haven't had any complaints yet.

38:10.850 --> 38:11.820
Here.

38:15.390 --> 38:19.690
I'm scared! I'm really scared of this!

38:31.810 --> 38:33.860
Well, see you tomorrow.

38:34.040 --> 38:36.530
Thank you for the fireworks.

38:37.380 --> 38:38.710
Good night.

38:42.320 --> 38:45.510
Tell Uncle that I'm
heading home right now.

38:47.990 --> 38:49.960
Thanks, ANN.

38:57.730 --> 38:59.100
Good work.

39:00.100 --> 39:01.290
Thank you.

39:02.340 --> 39:05.030
I didn't know you were a minor.

39:07.010 --> 39:09.170
Please don't tell the school.

39:10.280 --> 39:12.040
What should I do...

39:15.280 --> 39:19.010
Um, I'll add a free drink next time.

39:19.690 --> 39:21.750
So please let me go.

39:22.320 --> 39:23.290
Please.

39:24.690 --> 39:27.020
Trying to bribe an officer?

39:27.630 --> 39:28.890
Officer?

39:29.760 --> 39:31.820
Why are you working there?

39:32.070 --> 39:34.190
Because I get paid a lot.

39:34.300 --> 39:37.570
Plus the manager is really nice.

39:38.100 --> 39:41.970
You know, adults are very
cunning and difficult to deal with.

39:42.080 --> 39:44.270
Don't let their outsides fool you.

39:44.380 --> 39:47.840
Plus I have a bad
feeling about this place.

39:49.050 --> 39:50.950
I'm going to quit.

39:51.320 --> 39:54.410
So please don't tell
the school anything.

39:55.520 --> 39:57.960
I won't tell them about your job.

39:58.060 --> 39:59.390
Really?

39:59.630 --> 40:01.920
But in return, well...

40:02.460 --> 40:03.430
Um...

40:05.830 --> 40:07.060
Would you...

40:07.930 --> 40:09.300
...go out with me?

40:09.400 --> 40:10.430
Really?

40:10.840 --> 40:12.600
How old is this guy?

40:12.710 --> 40:14.870
I don't know, but maybe...

40:15.540 --> 40:17.840
...his late twenties?

40:18.850 --> 40:21.370
You don't mind dating older guys?

40:21.480 --> 40:24.140
They're much better
than guys my age.

40:24.250 --> 40:26.380
And you agreed?

40:27.890 --> 40:30.910
Anyway,
why is a cop interested in you?

40:33.490 --> 40:35.790
Where'd you meet a cop?

40:36.400 --> 40:38.330
You're hiding something, Monaka.

40:38.730 --> 40:41.830
This ice cream is so good.

40:42.900 --> 40:44.390
Fishy.

40:45.410 --> 40:46.570
Very fishy.

41:07.590 --> 41:09.460
It's not my fault...

41:09.730 --> 41:11.290
It's not my fault.

41:11.400 --> 41:12.420
Doi.

41:14.300 --> 41:17.430
Looks like you brought
home a terrible creature.

41:18.810 --> 41:21.430
Then there really is one more?

41:25.880 --> 41:26.810
Bye-bye!

41:26.880 --> 41:28.040
See you!

41:30.620 --> 41:31.950
Wait for me!

41:42.700 --> 41:44.320
Your next job.

41:44.430 --> 41:47.490
But the older twin
brother is still around.

41:47.600 --> 41:51.230
There have been dismembered
bodies these past few days.

41:51.340 --> 41:52.830
Did you know?

41:52.940 --> 41:55.570
I heard rumors about that in class.

41:56.180 --> 41:59.870
The Kudryavka's escape pod
crash-landed in Odaiba...

41:59.980 --> 42:04.210
...and it seems these cases
involve one of the survivors.

42:04.320 --> 42:05.280
Come on!

42:05.390 --> 42:08.010
The target is armed and dangerous.

42:08.120 --> 42:10.990
So equip yourself
with the best weapons...

42:11.090 --> 42:13.420
...and dispose of this target promptly.

42:13.530 --> 42:17.620
Why is the survivor
doing this all of a sudden?

42:19.670 --> 42:22.130
That's none of our business.

42:23.040 --> 42:27.770
It seems the target is on the move,
so I'll let you know the site by mail.

42:27.940 --> 42:29.000
Bye!

42:29.110 --> 42:30.370
Moving?

42:30.480 --> 42:34.000
Like there's somewhere specific.

42:37.650 --> 42:39.310
Oh, nice catch!

42:39.420 --> 42:41.720
Sorry! Are you okay?

42:42.120 --> 42:45.820
Sputnik, why did
you call me out today?

42:49.300 --> 42:52.360
I wanted to tell you
"happy birthday" in person.

42:52.870 --> 42:54.330
Oh, please...

42:55.700 --> 42:58.170
That bracelet looks nice.

42:58.270 --> 43:00.300
Is it from your boyfriend?

43:02.980 --> 43:04.370
She ignored me.

43:06.550 --> 43:07.810
Boyfriend...

43:08.050 --> 43:10.140
Would you go outwith me?

43:13.750 --> 43:15.190
Ouch...

43:36.910 --> 43:38.430
It's around here.

44:06.370 --> 44:09.240
You must really love that gun.

44:10.610 --> 44:16.410
That "red club" was made by my
friend long ago. It's a gun of destiny.

44:16.880 --> 44:18.410
Destiny?

44:19.150 --> 44:24.450
It belonged to some assassin,
one in the late teens.

44:24.560 --> 44:26.150
And a chick.

44:26.730 --> 44:28.250
Like you.

44:30.030 --> 44:34.590
But all of a sudden, that chick
disappeared several years ago.

44:34.700 --> 44:39.160
My friend died around
the same time as well.

44:39.370 --> 44:40.670
I see.

44:54.350 --> 44:55.910
Amazing!

44:56.520 --> 44:58.990
What was her name?

44:59.430 --> 45:01.190
What was it now...

45:31.260 --> 45:34.890
How dare you kill my brother!

45:36.900 --> 45:40.360
I can't believe you
showed yourself like this...

45:40.470 --> 45:44.330
By the way, we're not
the ones who killed your brother.

45:45.240 --> 45:49.370
You can talk nonsense
after you've apologized to him.

45:49.480 --> 45:53.810
The Angel of Death
killed your crazy brother.

45:55.450 --> 45:58.320
So it was the infamous assassin?

45:58.420 --> 46:02.350
Even if that's true,
you people still cornered him!

46:03.320 --> 46:06.350
The Angel of Death
is gonna get you too.

46:06.860 --> 46:07.990
Die.

46:08.230 --> 46:13.220
South America?
I recently saw this cool anime.

46:13.330 --> 46:15.630
Really? Changing the subject?

46:15.770 --> 46:18.170
Are you listening to what I'm saying?

46:18.270 --> 46:19.570
Bastard!

46:26.050 --> 46:28.210
Who would? Are you listening?

46:28.310 --> 46:29.280
Are you?

46:29.350 --> 46:30.610
I am. I am.

46:31.720 --> 46:33.340
You won't get away.

46:36.460 --> 46:37.580
Worried?

46:37.990 --> 46:43.390
Of course! You're telling me that a
mere assassin can get the job done?

46:44.260 --> 46:46.700
This is the best choice for us.

46:47.100 --> 46:50.590
We're talking about
the Angel of Death, you know.

46:50.700 --> 46:54.870
I don't care if it's an angel
or a devil. Just get the job done.

46:54.970 --> 46:56.170
Jeez...

47:37.450 --> 47:38.780
Bulletproof?

47:38.880 --> 47:41.180
What is that thing anyway?

48:19.430 --> 48:20.790
What is this thing?

48:28.700 --> 48:30.860
It doesn't want to fight?

48:43.920 --> 48:47.280
Not deep enough.
The explosive bullets have no effect.

48:48.690 --> 48:51.320
What are you people
doing this late at night?

49:22.150 --> 49:24.250
I'm sure it has a weak spot.

49:46.480 --> 49:49.010
Too bad I missed.

50:17.610 --> 50:19.870
W-What is it? What happened?

50:20.550 --> 50:22.040
It's that monster!

50:50.740 --> 50:52.010
Come on!

50:54.480 --> 50:57.010
Thank you so much! You saved us!

50:57.120 --> 50:59.020
I'm really thankful!

51:06.230 --> 51:08.090
What was that thing?

51:08.890 --> 51:12.590
J-Just between you and me,
that monster was once human...

51:12.700 --> 51:18.190
...a transformed crew member
from the ISS space station.

51:19.740 --> 51:23.230
There was some sort
of accident on the ISS.

51:23.940 --> 51:26.640
The space station's crew member...

51:26.980 --> 51:34.010
Plus they said it was caused by my
space food and radiation from the sun.

51:34.350 --> 51:39.790
If this was made public, my reputation
would've been ruined for good.

51:40.760 --> 51:44.790
Though I wanted that monster
to be disposed of discreetly...

51:50.270 --> 51:55.900
But it's amazing that a girl took
care of that monster all by herself.

51:56.610 --> 51:58.410
Which crew member?

51:58.510 --> 51:59.770
Want to know?

51:59.880 --> 52:04.820
The doctor said two people
transformed, but the name I heard...

52:06.290 --> 52:07.750
...was Orudo Noguchi.

52:09.150 --> 52:11.680
I forgot to ask about the other one.

52:11.790 --> 52:15.780
I don't know if that monster
was Noguchi or not.

52:16.930 --> 52:20.890
The other monster was blown
to bits on the Kudryavka.

52:26.670 --> 52:28.640
No... No...

52:28.710 --> 52:30.680
It can't be my dad!

52:32.080 --> 52:33.510
W-What?

52:33.680 --> 52:36.650
Are you Monaka?

52:37.550 --> 52:39.850
You're kidding, right? For real?

52:46.960 --> 52:48.760
Who were these people?

52:48.860 --> 52:53.360
A-Agents for some
organization hired by Defy Foods...

52:53.470 --> 52:58.700
They came pretending to be NASA
investigators to control the situation.

52:59.340 --> 53:00.830
To kill me too?

53:00.940 --> 53:04.140
I didn't know about it! It's true!

53:04.410 --> 53:05.710
Who are you?

53:06.180 --> 53:09.670
I-I'm Koichi Doi,
an employee of Defy Foods.

53:09.780 --> 53:10.910
Doi...

53:12.180 --> 53:15.350
You're the one who
sent my dad's packages.

53:15.790 --> 53:18.350
Then you really are Monaka...

53:24.860 --> 53:27.860
Damn... Where did he go?

53:31.100 --> 53:32.370
Dad...

53:36.010 --> 53:37.070
Stay still.

53:37.180 --> 53:38.440
Let me go!

53:38.540 --> 53:41.010
If you make a sound, I'll kill you...

53:45.180 --> 53:46.980
Tsuin! Freeze!

53:47.090 --> 53:48.490
Tsuin?

53:48.590 --> 53:50.020
You freeze!

53:50.720 --> 53:52.320
I'll kill this chick!

53:53.190 --> 53:55.820
You crazy brothers
do the same thing!

53:56.660 --> 53:58.060
That voice...

53:59.000 --> 54:00.490
Drop your gun!

54:00.730 --> 54:01.960
Bastard...

54:02.200 --> 54:05.660
Hurry up and drop it! I'll shoot her.

54:09.110 --> 54:10.970
Stay right there.

54:11.080 --> 54:12.240
Ow!

54:20.290 --> 54:21.280
Tsuin!

54:21.390 --> 54:22.850
Y-You're...

54:28.030 --> 54:30.020
Tsuin! Answer me!

54:37.900 --> 54:38.870
This is...

54:57.360 --> 54:59.120
Hey, it's regenerating!

54:59.220 --> 55:00.390
What?

55:57.380 --> 56:03.620
l got tired from playing all day.

56:04.190 --> 56:10.130
Silence somewhat
makes me feel comfortable.

56:10.230 --> 56:16.660
1 want to keep on
remembering what you look like.

56:17.070 --> 56:23.770
Even when I become an adult,
I still want to keep going on like this.

56:35.850 --> 56:42.120
I'm thinking in the sky high above.

56:42.660 --> 56:48.570
Even though there's no name,
I think about unimportant things.

56:48.670 --> 56:54.870
It's looping while I think.

56:55.440 --> 57:01.970
Things that l might forget tomorrow.

57:02.080 --> 57:07.680
l want you to keep on watching me.

57:08.620 --> 57:14.350
Keep on watching me.

57:14.630 --> 57:20.930
People who come back
and people who greet them.

57:21.030 --> 57:27.100
People who live inside my heart.

57:27.470 --> 57:33.900
We can feel each other
with the same temperature.

57:34.580 --> 57:42.450
You were always
there inside my heart.

57:43.460 --> 57:46.390
My sweet home...
